<onlyinclude>A '''knowledge market''' is an arrangement through which people or organizations exchange access to information, expertise, research or other knowledge-related resources. Exchange may involve money, reputation, reciprocal assistance or institutional incentives.

== Explanation ==
Examples include consulting, expert-question platforms, patent licensing and informal exchanges of expertise among colleagues. A market can help match someone who has a question with someone who has relevant knowledge. Payment and popularity do not establish that the answer is accurate.

